  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black woman in a white dress, seemingly in a theatrical or staged setting with other costumed individuals. The overlaid text reads: 'call me a hater if you want but,... when is the last time you saw a photo of anyone but a muslim holding a human head?' This text is a hateful and inflammatory statement that uses a grotesque and violent metaphor to target Muslims, implying that Muslims are uniquely associated with violence or barbarism by suggesting they are the only ones depicted holding a human head. This is a direct attack based on religion (Islamophobia) and racialized stereotypes, as it links the group to extreme violence. The meme uses the visual of a Black woman (who is not visibly Muslim) juxtaposed with the hateful text to create a false association or to imply that the woman is somehow complicit or representative of the stereotype. The intent is to provoke outrage or fear by weaponizing a violent image and associating it with a specific religious group, which is a form of hate speech and harmful propaganda. The meme is designed to incite prejudice and reinforce negative stereotypes about Muslims, making it clearly hateful and potentially harmful to the Muslim community.",
